      ],
      "focus": "Assess material and territorial scope; the treatment-related processing and sensitive genetic and health information; consent and information requirements; outward-transfer rules including recognised territories, approved clauses, and specific-situation derogations; security and any impact-assessment requirements. Consider whether Subregion A1 provisions should be examined by delegation."
    },
    {
      "corpus": "region_b",
      "engaged": true,
      "reason": "The recipient is established in Region B, the referral is stored and accessed there, and Harrow will receive and use the patient's health information in its own clinical record for care. Region B law could therefore apply to the recipient's receipt, use, security, retention, and access to the records.",
